  "note": "A long RN16 deck rises over the Paraná River to twin split-leg concrete pylons. Two planes of cable stays support the main spans. The approach viaduct, red triangular fenders, sidewalks and curved Corrientes landing remain distinct at viewing scale. The two skewed road joints meet the sampled RN16 approaches. The deck rises to clear the mapped Paraná water and pier bases extend below the standard terrain. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
